Description: epiPortrait is a replicate-aware computational framework for
    quantitative phenotyping and comparison of epigenomic domains from
    normalized continuous signal tracks and per-sample native peak/domain
    calls (histone-mark ChIP-seq / CUT&Tag as the primary use case; also
    applicable to ATAC-seq-derived domains). It characterizes each shared
    genomic domain by integrated signal magnitude (Intensity),
    sample-specific native peak breadth geometry, and continuous
    within-domain signal architecture (SignalDispersion). Replicate-level
    evidence is retained explicitly and aggregated with transparent support
    rules, enabling condition-specific classification of Intensity-Super,
    Breadth-Super, Dual-Super, Typical, or Uncertain domain states without
    using the consensus-domain width as the breadth caller. The package
    further supports condition transitions, continuous domain-width
    remodeling, signal quality control, genome-aware domain annotation,
    optional BEDPE contact evidence, expression-aware candidate-gene
    prioritization, and publication-oriented visualization.
